  <entry>
    <title>Best Practices for Git Workflows in Monorepo</title>
    <link href="http://quanru.github.io/2022/12/31/Best-Practices-for-Git-Workflows-in-Monorepo/"/>
    <id>http://quanru.github.io/2022/12/31/Best-Practices-for-Git-Workflows-in-Monorepo/</id>
    <published>2022-12-31T08:48:15.000Z</published>
    <updated>2026-03-15T15:56:15.000Z</updated>
    
    
    <summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;No single Git workflow is a silver bullet. The right Git workflow often depends on the project’s code scale, number of collaborators, and use cases. This article starts with the Feature branch workflow suitable for small Monorepos, then covers the Trunk-based workflow for medium-to-large Monorepos, and provides selection criteria for reference. Hopefully, you’ll find the right Git workflow for your Monorepo!&lt;/p&gt;</summary>
    
    
    
